OL,3,GNEWSAHow a reservoir is helping to save
OL,4,Adeclining bird
OL,5,
OL,6,FOnce a thriving and common feature of
OL,7,Four woodlands, the willow tit is now
OL,8,Fthe UK's fastest declining resident
OL,9,Fbird.
OL,11,FAccording to Severn Trent Water,
OL,12,Fnumbers have fallen by about 96% from
OL,13,F1967 to 2023, with only around 3,400
OL,14,Fbreeding pairs left across the whole
OL,15,Fcountry.
OL,17,FApproximately 10 of those are believed
OL,18,Fto nest in the grounds of Tittesworth
OL,19,FReservoir, near Leek in Staffordshire.
OL,23,APub: 03-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
